TWO LICENCES, DELIBERATELY

Code and quiz content are licensed separately, because they are used
differently and a single licence would serve one badly.

  Code      Apache License 2.0            LICENSE
            Everything that is not a quiz pack: the validator, the
            scripts, and any engine code added later.

  Content   Creative Commons Attribution  packs/*.yaml
            4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
            The quiz packs. Each pack declares its own `license:` and
            `source:` fields, which are authoritative for that pack.

Apache-2.0 is the wrong instrument for prose — it speaks of source, object
form and derivative works — and CC licences are the wrong instrument for
code. Attribution for reused questions is what CC-BY provides and what the
packs need; a patent grant and an NOTICE requirement are what the code needs.

A pack that carries a different `license:` value is governed by that value,
not by this file. Packs incorporating third-party material may be CC-BY-SA
where the upstream source requires it.

